t></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android Watch 14, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Improper input validation in FacAtFunction in Galaxy Watch prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local attacker to execute arbitrary code with system privilege.<br>The patch adds proper check logic.</font></div><br><br><strong><font size="5"> Moderate </font><br></strong><br> <div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2025-2186(CVE-2026-21021)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Improper input validation in Routines prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows physical attackers to launch privileged activity.<br>The patch adds proper check logic.</font></div><br><div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2026-0086(CVE-2026-21015)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 14, 15, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Incorrect default permissions in FactoryCamera prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local attacker to access unique identifier.<br>The patch adds proper access control.</font></div><br><div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2026-0230(CVE-2026-21016)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 14, 15, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Incorrect privilege assignment in LocationManager prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local attackers to access sensitive information.<br>The patch adds proper validation logic.</font></div><br><div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2026-0252(CVE-2026-21022)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 15, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Improper handling of insufficient permissions in Routines prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local attackers to access sensitive information.<br>The patch adds proper check logic.</font></div><br><div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2026-0478(CVE-2026-21018)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 14, 15, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Out-of-bounds write in SveService prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local privileged attackers to execute arbitrary code.<br>The patch adds proper input validation.</font></div><br><div style="padding-left:20px">    <strong><font size="4" style="line-height:2.5">SVE-2026-0623(CVE-2026-21020)</font></strong><font size="3"><br>Affected versions: Android 14, 15, 16<br>Disclosure status: Privately disclosed<br>Improper export of android application components in OmaCP prior to SMR May-2026 Release 1 allows local attackers to trigger privileged functions.<br>The patch adds proper permission.</font></div><br><br><em>Some SVE items included in the Samsung Android Security Update cannot be disclosed at this time.</em>
